  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given curves are $y=x^3$ and $y=\\sqrt{x}$\nBoth curves intersects at $x=0$ and $x=1$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/z_KznZMe4vfzCzaJXSNJ_XvekF3NnRaPnjhDPnsu5nk.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nShaded region is required area\n$\\begin{aligned}\nA & =\\left|\\int_0^1\\left(x^3-\\sqrt{x}\\right) d x\\right|=\\left|\\left[\\frac{x^4}{4}-\\frac{2 x^{3 / 2}}{3}\\right]_0^1\\right| \\\\\n& =\\left|\\left[\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}\\right]\\right| \\\\\n& =\\frac{5}{12} \\text { sq. unit }\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
